-- title:
--   Artinian universality from square-zero universality
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a field $k$ of characteristic $q$, and a complete discrete valuation domain $W_0$ whose maximal ideal is generated by $q$, together with a surjective ring map $\mathrm{res}_0 : W_0 \to k$ whose kernel is the maximal ideal of $W_0$. Let $F_0$ be a one-dimensional commutative formal group law over $k$ satisfying `F₀.IsDrinfeldBasisAdic ⊥ q 0 0`, that is, with the ideal $\bot$ taken as the ambient ideal, there is a unit $u$ in $k[[X]]$ with $F_0$'s $q$-th series equal to $u$ times `F₀.drinfeldDivisor q 0 0`. Let $F_u$ be a commutative formal group law over $W_0[[X]]$ whose base change along $\mathrm{res}_0 \circ \mathrm{constantCoeff}$ is $F_0$, i.e. the two-variable power series of $F_0$ is the image of that of $F_u$ under this map. Call a pair $(T, \mathrm{res}_T)$ admissible when $T$ is an Artinian local $W_0$-algebra and $\mathrm{res}_T : T \to k$ is surjective with kernel the maximal ideal of $T$ and agrees with $\mathrm{res}_0$ on $W_0$; and consider, for admissible $(T,\mathrm{res}_T)$ and a commutative formal group law $G$ over $T$ whose associated series is the image of that of $F_0$ under $\mathrm{res}_T$, the assertion that there is a unique $W_0$-algebra map $\varphi : W_0[[X]] \to T$ with $\mathrm{res}_T(\varphi(r)) = \mathrm{res}_0(\mathrm{constantCoeff}\, r)$ for all $r$, admitting a formal group law $G'$ over $T$ that is the base change of $F_u$ along $\varphi$ and an isomorphism of laws $\psi : G' \to G$ (a power series with zero constant term and unit linear coefficient satisfying the compatibility with the two laws) all of whose coefficients reduce under $\mathrm{res}_T$ to those of $X$. The theorem asserts that if this holds for every admissible $(T,\mathrm{res}_T)$ with $(\mathrm{maximalIdeal}\,T)^2 = \bot$ and $q = 0$ in $T$, then it holds for every admissible $(T,\mathrm{res}_T)$ whatsoever.
--
--   This is the inductive step upgrading square-zero (tangent-level) universality of the lift $F_u$ over $W_0[[X]]$ to the full Lubin–Tate universal property of $W_0[[X]]$ as deformation ring of a formal group law with Drinfeld basis datum, over all Artinian local $W_0$-algebras with residue field $k$. It feeds [`FormalGroup.IsDrinfeldBasisAdic.universal_deformation_powerSeries_of_generic_lift`](thm.html#FormalGroup.IsDrinfeldBasisAdic.universal_deformation_powerSeries_of_generic_lift), and uses the small-extension square-zero lifting statement together with the transport of homomorphisms of laws along base change.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_FormalGroup_IsDrinfeldBasisAdic_universal_of_universal_sq_zero.lean

